Subject: [PATCH] vrend: per-render-target blend and color-mask calls stop at GL_MAX_DRAW_BUFFERS

vrend sets the blend and color-mask state of each render target with indexed GL calls
(glBlendFuncSeparateiARB, glBlendEquationSeparateiARB, glEnableIndexedEXT/glDisableIndexedEXT,
glColorMaskIndexedEXT). Three loops (vrend_hw_emit_blend, and the color-mask set and restore
around vrend_clear) run over PIPE_MAX_COLOR_BUFS (8) targets. On a GLES driver with
GL_MAX_DRAW_BUFFERS below 8 (Mali-G52 r26p0 in the Galaxy A32: 4), the calls for the indices
from GL_MAX_DRAW_BUFFERS up are GL_INVALID_VALUE (OpenGL ES 3.2, the index must be below
GL_MAX_DRAW_BUFFERS). A draw into 2 or more color buffers sets independent_blend_enable, so it
runs these loops and fails with error 1281 at DRAW_VBO.

The loops now stop at vrend_state.max_draw_buffers (read from GL_MAX_DRAW_BUFFERS at start-up,
at most 8). On a host with 8 the loops are the same as before.

Written for virglrenderer e18f8c00 src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c.

---
--- a/src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c
+++ b/src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c
@@ -4720,7 +4720,7 @@
       if (sub_ctx->hw_blend_state.independent_blend_enable &&
           has_feature(feat_indep_blend)) {
          int i;
-         for (i = 0; i < PIPE_MAX_COLOR_BUFS; i++)
+         for (i = 0; i < vrend_state.max_draw_buffers; i++)
             glColorMaskIndexedEXT(i, GL_TRUE, GL_TRUE, GL_TRUE, GL_TRUE);
       } else
          glColorMask(GL_TRUE, GL_TRUE, GL_TRUE, GL_TRUE);
@@ -4774,7 +4774,7 @@
       if (sub_ctx->hw_blend_state.independent_blend_enable &&
           has_feature(feat_indep_blend)) {
          int i;
-         for (i = 0; i < PIPE_MAX_COLOR_BUFS; i++) {
+         for (i = 0; i < vrend_state.max_draw_buffers; i++) {
             struct pipe_blend_state *blend = &sub_ctx->hw_blend_state;
             glColorMaskIndexedEXT(i, blend->rt[i].colormask & PIPE_MASK_R ? GL_TRUE : GL_FALSE,
                                   blend->rt[i].colormask & PIPE_MASK_G ? GL_TRUE : GL_FALSE,
@@ -6436,7 +6436,7 @@
       /* ARB_draw_buffers_blend is required for this */
       int i;

-      for (i = 0; i < PIPE_MAX_COLOR_BUFS; i++) {
+      for (i = 0; i < vrend_state.max_draw_buffers; i++) {

          if (state->rt[i].blend_enable) {
             bool dual_src = util_blend_state_is_dual(&sub_ctx->blend_state, i);
